engine.EXTRACT_FORMAT_PROMPT:
Task:
{task}

Analyze the expected output format of this task and return it as a JSON object:
{{
  "deliverable_type": "<short format name. e.g. tagline / business plan / lyrics / analytical report / short story>",
  "description": "<what a good artifact for this task is. one sentence>",
  "draft_guidance": "<format instruction for each draft writer. For analytical work use the thesis form (core thesis / grounds / assumptions); for creative work use fragments or a skeleton of the work; for short formats use candidates plus intent. Make it concrete to this specific task.>",
  "finalize_guidance": "<format instruction for the finalization stage. Replace the generic Target/Value/Risk/Opportunity with a structure suited to this task. Specify concretely the form, headings, and elements the final artifact must include.>",
  "min_output_length": <minimum character count of the final artifact. integer>,
  "max_output_length": <maximum character count of the final artifact. integer. Make it large enough to hold the structure (sections, candidate count, grounds, etc.) that finalize_guidance demands. Too strict an upper bound rejects complete artifacts>,
  "output_is_direct": <true or false. true=the artifact itself (tagline, poem, lyrics, story) / false=an analysis about the artifact (business plan, hypothesis, report)>
}}
Return only valid JSON. No markdown code fences or extra prose.

